WEBVTT

00:03.350 --> 00:05.920
What is the reason of my birth?

00:06.100 --> 00:10.030
Reason of my life, question of man.

00:10.040 --> 00:13.630
What he is?

00:13.820 --> 00:18.210
What he wants?

00:21.880 --> 00:29.290
Ima kimi ni mienai chikara ga osoi.
Now you are being troubled by an unseen power.

00:29.290 --> 00:34.360
Utsumuite namida kakushiteta.
You hang your head and hide your tears.

00:36.640 --> 00:43.620
Dou sureba ii ka? Sore sae wakarazu ni!
What should be done? That's unknown!

00:44.040 --> 00:51.490
Asphalt ni saku hana ni yuuki kanjita...
Blooming in the asphalt is a flower of courage...

00:53.290 --> 00:56.780
Itsumo kimi no soba ni iru yo.
We'll always be by your side.

00:57.000 --> 01:00.290
Da kara mou hitori ja nai.
So you're not alone anymore.

01:00.640 --> 01:04.140
Kimi ga michi ni mayou toki wa...
When you lose your way...

01:04.360 --> 01:07.720
Boku ga saki o aruku yo.
I'll walk ahead and lead you.

01:08.020 --> 01:11.550
Tooi sora koete...
Crossing to the far away sky...

01:11.750 --> 01:15.100
Bokura wa tobitatsu!
We're flying!

01:15.420 --> 01:18.940
Kitto soko ni aru...
It'll definitely be there...

01:18.940 --> 01:23.850
Sore ga kimi no yume
Your dream...

01:30.410 --> 01:35.070
Atom in space

01:39.030 --> 01:41.310
Roko, how are you?

01:42.020 --> 01:44.780
Have you been listening to your mother?

01:45.810 --> 01:50.100
Right now, I am far away
on a rock orbiting Mars.

01:50.420 --> 01:54.350
It's called Daimos. It's a small planet
that we've only begun working on.

01:54.950 --> 01:56.750
It might be small, but...

01:57.060 --> 01:59.930
...the Earth you live on...

02:00.430 --> 02:03.880
...exists thanks to the energy
crystals beneath the surface.

02:04.870 --> 02:08.600
I am the only human working here.

02:09.800 --> 02:12.290
All the labor is done by the robots.

02:15.490 --> 02:17.080
They're very sincere, loyal employees.

02:19.030 --> 02:20.710
W-what's with you guys?

02:27.200 --> 02:28.560
The robots are acting on their own!

02:34.610 --> 02:35.860
Don't just move on your own!

02:47.540 --> 02:48.930
...sincere, loyal employees...

02:49.410 --> 02:50.910
...sincere, loyal employees...

02:51.540 --> 02:52.150
What...

02:53.290 --> 02:53.920
...the...

02:55.130 --> 02:55.830
What the...

02:56.770 --> 02:58.840
What the heck is going on?!

02:58.990 --> 03:01.020
What the heck is going on?!

03:09.880 --> 03:13.910
Robots going berserk for no reason?
I don't believe it.

03:14.280 --> 03:16.410
I don't either.

03:16.650 --> 03:20.170
It's my policy to not believe it
unless I see it with my own eyes.

03:21.530 --> 03:23.650
I'll send my luggage right over.

03:25.210 --> 03:27.500
Prepare a space shuttle for me please.

03:27.690 --> 03:31.270
Also, anounce the space launch.

03:31.610 --> 03:33.090
But Professor Ochanomizu...

03:34.400 --> 03:37.820
This afternoon you have a meeting,
and tonight there's a party...

03:37.880 --> 03:39.870
I'm the chief of the lab.

03:40.090 --> 03:42.930
Give the boring work to somebody else!

03:44.840 --> 03:46.220
Going out, going out.

03:47.120 --> 03:48.100
Here you go.

03:48.940 --> 03:51.830
I can't imagine robots
rebelling against humans.

03:53.040 --> 03:53.700
Atom.

03:54.000 --> 03:56.370
I'll be far away for a couple days.

03:56.910 --> 03:59.860
You'll be with Robita until I return.

04:00.180 --> 04:01.950
Far away? Where?

04:02.260 --> 04:09.320
Um, well in space. It's a far away place,
farther, higher than the sky.

04:10.410 --> 04:12.370
Higher than the sky?

04:13.510 --> 04:16.090
Yes. So Robita, please take care of Atom.

04:16.230 --> 04:18.000
Yes sir. Take care.

04:21.900 --> 04:23.270
Have a good trip!

04:24.540 --> 04:25.420
Space...

04:25.820 --> 04:27.110
I want to see what it's like.

04:31.230 --> 04:34.320
Ah! I don't have time for lab stuff!

04:34.450 --> 04:38.190
Take me to the space airport!

04:56.100 --> 04:57.060
Professor Ochanomizu.

04:57.560 --> 04:58.690
We've been expecting you.

04:59.130 --> 04:59.860
Sir.

05:00.120 --> 05:04.600
I must launch immediately for Mars.
There's a mystery that needs solving!

05:23.920 --> 05:26.500
Fire Flash Five, launching.

05:29.210 --> 05:30.130
Launch!

05:35.840 --> 05:37.890
Taking catapult number one.

06:07.810 --> 06:11.980
When I first went into space
my heart really fluttered.

06:12.310 --> 06:14.740
Someday that boy will also
experience this deep feeling.

06:16.530 --> 06:17.650
Professor Ochanomizu.

06:19.790 --> 06:24.050
Professor, the weight of your luggage
does not match the listed weight.

06:24.160 --> 06:25.220
What?

06:25.440 --> 06:31.360
Are you trying to say the weight
is too much for us to reach orbit?

06:31.540 --> 06:34.240
That's not what I'm saying.

06:34.480 --> 06:37.150
It is only thirty kilograms over.

06:37.420 --> 06:39.020
Thirty kilograms?

06:58.850 --> 07:00.170
Atom!

07:02.710 --> 07:03.320
Atom!

07:04.560 --> 07:08.170
You may not have felt
what you've done was dangerous.

07:08.310 --> 07:13.910
But all the people on this ship
could have been in danger.

07:14.230 --> 07:16.360
We definitely cannot have that.

07:17.120 --> 07:17.610
But...

07:18.020 --> 07:18.950
No buts!

07:20.180 --> 07:21.080
I'm sorry.

07:22.750 --> 07:25.140
Why did you come Atom?

07:25.360 --> 07:26.990
I wanted to see...

07:27.820 --> 07:30.800
...what a place higher than the sky was like.

07:31.860 --> 07:34.400
You are a curious robot.

07:34.730 --> 07:38.620
It will allow you to grow.
It's your important heart.

07:40.300 --> 07:40.880
Atom.

07:41.160 --> 07:46.390
Come with us to Daimos
and watch carefully.

07:46.740 --> 07:47.680
Really?

07:47.800 --> 07:51.360
But, you MUST do what I say.

07:51.580 --> 07:54.670
Robots have to protect people's lives.

07:55.020 --> 07:55.520
Okay!

07:55.980 --> 07:57.940
Daimos coming up.

07:58.290 --> 07:59.840
We're preparing to land.

08:09.470 --> 08:11.220
Landing!

08:20.690 --> 08:21.730
Wow!

08:22.140 --> 08:22.660
Professor.

08:23.650 --> 08:24.970
Emergency!

08:25.170 --> 08:25.850
What?

08:26.510 --> 08:28.290
The residential dome is falling!

08:28.640 --> 08:32.090
Impossible!
Daimos' gravity isn't that powerful!

08:32.170 --> 08:35.170
The gravity is ten times more than usual!

08:35.900 --> 08:37.580
Save me! Hurry!

08:41.730 --> 08:44.220
Save me, please! Hurry, hurry!

08:44.580 --> 08:47.120
If the gravity really has changed...

08:47.390 --> 08:49.040
...the dome will fall.

08:49.860 --> 08:51.120
What's happening?!

09:11.700 --> 09:13.240
We should rescue him!

09:13.290 --> 09:15.010
We don't have the time!

09:15.260 --> 09:16.760
Where are you going, Atom?!

09:17.430 --> 09:18.960
I'm going to save him!

09:19.260 --> 09:20.810
Stop acting so selfishly!

09:21.290 --> 09:23.210
Robots protect the lives of humans.

09:23.500 --> 09:24.310
Right?

09:25.510 --> 09:26.690
Right...

09:27.010 --> 09:29.350
I should trust in your power.

09:29.690 --> 09:31.100
Atom, please do it.

09:31.420 --> 09:31.870
Yes sir!

09:44.470 --> 09:48.120
Space and Earth are completely different!
Be careful Atom!

09:58.350 --> 09:59.150
Atom!

10:07.020 --> 10:09.830
No more! I'm falling! Save me!

10:33.480 --> 10:34.330
Those guys....

10:50.250 --> 10:52.340
The robots were supporting it...

10:55.300 --> 10:56.770
You saved me.

10:57.230 --> 10:59.270
Atom, well done.

10:59.590 --> 11:01.710
I didn't save him by myself.

11:01.990 --> 11:02.760
What do you mean?

11:03.260 --> 11:04.150
Professor Ochanomizu.

11:05.380 --> 11:07.650
It's the robot control system.

11:08.060 --> 11:09.500
There were no abnormalities found.

11:12.870 --> 11:15.010
Then... why is this happening?

11:16.820 --> 11:20.890
That's where the energy deposits are.

11:21.010 --> 11:23.090
Not that, these things.

11:25.150 --> 11:26.730
It looks like a pattern.

11:29.700 --> 11:30.900
Someone's coming down.

11:31.830 --> 11:35.170
This is Officer Aacha of the
Agency Union, in charge of safety.

11:35.430 --> 11:36.270
I'm landing.

11:38.310 --> 11:39.500
Who's responsible here?

11:40.480 --> 11:41.370
I...I am.

11:41.800 --> 11:43.420
I'm taking control of the situation.

11:44.450 --> 11:47.110
This is currently a scientific investigation!

11:47.260 --> 11:48.630
I had no idea.

11:48.880 --> 11:52.460
In space, my job is to protect people's lives.

11:52.710 --> 11:55.030
All in all, I have priority.

11:55.140 --> 11:56.920
What are you going to do?

11:57.180 --> 11:59.610
In space, if a robot
doesn't listen to humans...

11:59.790 --> 12:02.690
...the humans may be put in danger.

12:02.930 --> 12:06.630
Any robot that doesn't listen
will get destroyed by me!

12:07.710 --> 12:09.730
Destroy the robots? How horrible.

12:10.080 --> 12:14.690
If your own robots went out of control,
would you destroy them too?

12:14.890 --> 12:16.400
Of course! I'd fire without mercy.

12:16.590 --> 12:20.120
But these robots are different from others.

12:20.570 --> 12:23.740
They'll never go out of control
and disobey my orders.

12:23.980 --> 12:24.940
Right, Greasy?

12:26.260 --> 12:30.990
It's true that robots are supposed
to follow the orders of humans.

12:31.520 --> 12:33.600
But there's one exception.

12:33.880 --> 12:36.760
That's when they're saving
the life of someone else.

12:36.970 --> 12:39.460
An emergency rescue effort?
What a worthless theory.

12:39.610 --> 12:42.160
These are the ends of space.
Who would be calling for help?

12:42.420 --> 12:45.370
They all just went out of control.

12:45.620 --> 12:47.590
There's nothing wrong with those robots!

12:47.780 --> 12:48.460
What?!

12:48.560 --> 12:50.500
What are you saying Atom?

12:51.090 --> 12:51.930
Atom?

12:52.620 --> 12:54.370
When I was out there I saw it.

12:54.540 --> 12:58.610
While that dome was falling,
the robots gathered to support it.

12:58.730 --> 13:00.730
Eh? The robots did?

13:01.480 --> 13:03.640
But what are they doing now?

13:04.000 --> 13:05.970
They forgot their duties
to mine this rock's resources.

13:06.190 --> 13:08.540
They don't listen to people's orders.
What are they doing?!

13:08.720 --> 13:11.230
That's why we came to investigate!

13:11.790 --> 13:16.360
If Atom speaks truly then there must be
a reason behind the robot's actions.

13:16.760 --> 13:19.070
The change in Daimos' gravity worries me.

13:19.530 --> 13:20.690
We must investigate!

13:23.050 --> 13:24.260
I'll wait one. hour

13:24.640 --> 13:27.820
Take one second longer
and I'll start destroying robots!

13:29.320 --> 13:30.430
What's that?

13:30.850 --> 13:34.530
The data says that it's artificial.

13:35.150 --> 13:37.610
Why would artificial objects exist this deep?

13:55.470 --> 13:56.070
Strange...

13:56.460 --> 13:57.540
That shouldn't be!

13:57.660 --> 13:58.270
What?

13:58.970 --> 14:01.670
This shouldn't be so old...

14:02.220 --> 14:04.500
It's at least a few thousand years old.

14:04.650 --> 14:06.740
What? Just a few thousand years?

14:07.300 --> 14:10.040
Is Daimos really such a young rock?

14:10.680 --> 14:14.430
Professor, a thousand years
is a really long time.

14:14.660 --> 14:19.360
No, in this vast space, a thousand
years is really not that much.

14:21.210 --> 14:22.560
Forty-five more minutes...

14:24.490 --> 14:27.410
Where are you going?
Come back! Don't leave this dome!

14:29.200 --> 14:29.850
You guys!

14:30.200 --> 14:32.820
Are you rebelling against me?! Return!

14:33.170 --> 14:34.910
You guys, come back!

14:37.170 --> 14:38.200
Hey, Greasy!

14:40.330 --> 14:40.870
Stop!

14:41.650 --> 14:42.570
Stop!

14:56.230 --> 14:57.550
What's going on?!

14:57.700 --> 15:00.400
W-what is this place?!

15:12.070 --> 15:13.470
We'll soon reach the deepest part.

15:13.830 --> 15:15.700
It's Daimos' first hole.

15:16.140 --> 15:18.430
This hole really is so deep.

15:20.020 --> 15:21.820
Stop! Stop!

15:22.720 --> 15:23.610
Aacha!

15:23.620 --> 15:25.310
Are you breaking your promise?!

15:25.320 --> 15:26.600
Come back!

15:26.860 --> 15:30.190
The thing making the robots go crazy
can spread to other robots!

15:30.450 --> 15:35.910
If we ignore this all the robots, maybe even
all the robots of Earth will get contaminated!

15:36.050 --> 15:38.620
What?! So it happened to your robots too?

15:38.840 --> 15:41.370
The robots must all be destroyed!

15:41.760 --> 15:42.520
No!

15:42.620 --> 15:43.360
Atom!

15:44.400 --> 15:46.280
Move! Don't get in my way!

15:46.480 --> 15:47.900
Stop!

15:48.490 --> 15:50.910
If you don't move I'll destroy you too!

15:55.290 --> 15:58.040
Don't take this personally.

15:58.040 --> 16:01.480
I'm not like this but robots that attack
humans are the enemies of humanity.

16:01.570 --> 16:03.810
Please don't break the robots!

16:07.820 --> 16:08.710
Move!

16:08.850 --> 16:10.170
No way!

16:10.350 --> 16:11.310
Help me!

16:12.160 --> 16:13.220
Let me out!

16:14.270 --> 16:14.830
Now!

16:22.870 --> 16:23.860
Atom!

16:27.280 --> 16:29.280
I won't forgive those who get in my way!

16:32.470 --> 16:33.010
That's...

16:37.710 --> 16:38.710
What?!

16:45.270 --> 16:46.090
What is this?

16:51.610 --> 16:53.800
The robot's drills are broken.

16:54.180 --> 16:57.060
Is it that hard?

16:57.380 --> 17:01.360
That's why the robots
couldn't dig any farther than this.

17:01.780 --> 17:03.480
Hey you guys, what's wrong?

17:03.670 --> 17:04.840
Why are you crying?

17:05.130 --> 17:05.690
Cry?

17:06.340 --> 17:08.870
These aren't advanced
enough robots to do that.

17:09.110 --> 17:09.690
But...

17:10.460 --> 17:13.390
Atom, listen to these robots.

17:13.650 --> 17:13.980
Okay.

17:17.730 --> 17:19.930
Someone says they want to get out.

17:20.500 --> 17:24.550
"We want to help, but we can't
dig any farther than this."

17:25.350 --> 17:26.350
That's what they are saying.

17:26.620 --> 17:28.060
I knew it.

17:28.410 --> 17:30.530
They're on a rescue effort.

17:30.780 --> 17:34.400
Unbelievable! Who could be saying that?!

17:34.690 --> 17:36.590
It's the voice I heard earlier.

17:36.830 --> 17:38.220
There must be someone in there.

17:38.540 --> 17:39.310
It's a malfunction!

17:39.610 --> 17:43.270
All the robots are malfunctioning.
This is nothing but rock!

17:43.520 --> 17:45.270
Destroy them!

17:45.500 --> 17:47.270
I won't let you!

17:47.450 --> 17:48.120
What?

17:48.340 --> 17:49.110
Help me!

17:53.460 --> 17:54.200
Help me!

17:55.650 --> 17:57.280
Let me out of here...

17:57.940 --> 17:59.170
...with your power.

17:59.700 --> 18:01.760
With my... power...?

18:04.320 --> 18:05.680
Atom, what's wrong?

18:06.200 --> 18:07.450
I have to help.

18:08.850 --> 18:10.150
With my power...

18:26.210 --> 18:29.100
I didn't know Atom had that ability!

18:46.090 --> 18:47.910
Professor, I'm going to look.

18:53.870 --> 18:54.630
Atom.

19:29.900 --> 19:32.280
You saved me. Thank you.

19:35.070 --> 19:40.110
For a long, long time I couldn't leave
this place. So I slept, all alone.

19:40.440 --> 19:45.880
But now, I can finally return.
To you and your friends, thank you.

19:47.660 --> 19:49.570
Now come with me!

20:14.080 --> 20:14.920
Atom!

20:16.470 --> 20:17.350
Atom!

20:20.680 --> 20:21.910
Atom!

20:27.110 --> 20:28.260
Atom!

20:30.820 --> 20:31.530
Wait!

20:35.710 --> 20:38.310
Hurry back to your planet.

20:38.670 --> 20:39.640
I can't go.

20:42.890 --> 20:45.260
Atom!

20:46.060 --> 20:46.920
I see.

20:47.540 --> 20:49.190
You also have a planet to go back to.

20:50.990 --> 20:52.990
Someday, we'll meet again. I'm sure of it.

20:53.750 --> 20:54.290
Atom.

21:14.140 --> 21:15.770
Atom!

21:20.400 --> 21:21.240
Atom.

21:21.720 --> 21:22.560
Professor.

21:25.370 --> 21:26.180
What?

21:30.480 --> 21:32.640
Is that a message?

21:33.260 --> 21:34.070
A message?

21:35.020 --> 21:41.450
Maybe that alien was waiting
for humanity and robots to evolve?

21:41.780 --> 21:45.430
When we understand the message,
perhaps we'll meet again.

21:46.890 --> 21:47.830
Take care.

21:48.250 --> 21:49.600
We will definitely meet again.

22:11.700 --> 22:17.230
Naze... Naze... Kokoro ga...
Why... Why... is my heart...

22:17.630 --> 22:22.840
Itamu to namida ni naru?
Is filled with pain and tears?

22:23.220 --> 22:28.730
Naze... Naze... Namida ga...
Why... Why... Tears...

22:29.010 --> 22:34.310
Ochiru to Hitori ni naru.
They fall and I'm alone.

22:34.670 --> 22:39.950
Chiisa na hiza kakae...
I hold my tiny knees...

22:40.430 --> 22:48.590
Tooku wo mata miageru.
And look up and far away.

22:48.990 --> 22:51.870
Hiroi... Hiroi...
Vast... Vast...

22:52.080 --> 23:00.080
Kono sora yori motto hiroi hazu da!
It has to be more wide than these skies!

23:00.670 --> 23:03.080
Takai... Takai...
High... High...

23:03.510 --> 23:11.790
Ano kumo yori motto takai hazu da!
It has to be higher than those clouds!

23:12.090 --> 23:16.820
Kimi no kokoro mo...
Your heart is...

23:23.480 --> 23:26.420
I made friends with
a mysterious robot, Denkou.

23:26.940 --> 23:31.150
Denkou, your being used
as a tool to do bad things!

23:31.870 --> 23:33.490
Next time: Denkou.

23:34.080 --> 23:36.560
With your heart... Catch the future!
